    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are the base and the log-capture helper), and it passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- A single-responsibility step that logs one line via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, carrying the owner id, the assigned `customerCode`, and the effective `registrationDate`.\n- It reads the persisted owner via `@Val Owner` (no mutation, pure side-effect) and does nothing else.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted the `audit` step between `save` and `respond`. Placing it after `SaveOwner` ensures the generated owner id is populated (\"on successful create\"), and it stays under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\nThe audit line reads e.g. `Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-21`. Since `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate`, its `toString()` is ISO-8601, matching the JSON serialization the test reads back \u2014 so the test's `anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` assertion holds. The full suite builds green.",
